2026-08-25T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-1025) 'Model memory arithmetic
 # uuid: 235882fc-d23e-5f3b-a1b4-9485446ebfea
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:attest-in:none
 RFD:Published  1 RFD
 Serials:Weftspun

2026-08-25T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-1025) 'capacity planning
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-1025) 'Size a machine from a model's parameter count.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-1025) 'RFD66606-1016 says what each model is. It does not say what each model costs.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-1025) 'Look up the model below, then apply the safe rule for one resident model.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-1025) 'Model memory arithmetic
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-1025) '- The load transient. A loader that reads the file into host memory,
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-1025) '  and then copies to the device, holds two copies. A loader that maps
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-1025) '  the file, and copies direct to the device, holds one copy.
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-1025) '- The runtime overhead. A CUDA context, the allocator, and the
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-1025) '  fragmentation add about 10 percent above the weights.
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-1025) '- The activation peak. This depends on the batch size, the resolution,
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-1025) '  and the step count. It does not depend on the parameter count.
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-1025) '
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-1025) 'The safe rule for one resident model is below.
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-1025) '
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-1025) '```
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-1025) 'device memory = weight GB x 1.1 + activation peak
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-1025) '```
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-1025) 'Compute the memory from the parameter count. Apply the rule to each catalog model, and
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-1025) 'treat the estimated rows as an upper bound for planning.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-1025) 'The rule
 # tags: rfd:section-heading
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-1025) 'bf16 holds one parameter in 2 bytes. The weight bytes are therefore
 # tags: rfd:section
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-1025) 'the parameter count multiplied by 2.
 # tags: rfd:section
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-1025) '
 # tags: rfd:section
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-1025) '```
 # tags: rfd:section
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-1025) 'weight bytes = parameters x 2
 # tags: rfd:section
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-1025) 'weight GB    = parameters in billions x 2
 # tags: rfd:section
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-1025) '```
 # tags: rfd:section
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-1025) '
 # tags: rfd:section
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-1025) 'This document counts 1 GB as 1,000,000,000 bytes. The GiB figure is
 # tags: rfd:section
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-1025) 'smaller by 7 percent.
 # tags: rfd:section
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-1025) 'RFD66606-1016 lists the models. RFD66606-1027 gives the totals and the consequence.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-1025) 'RFD66606-1030 breaks down the See-Through row. RFD66606-1034 checks the rule against a
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-1025) 'measured model.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-1025) 'bf16 memory per model
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-1025) 'Prefer `measured` over every other source, and prefer bf16 over fp16 where a checkpoint
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-1025) 'offers both. The two formats cost the same memory, and bf16 carries the wider exponent
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-1025) 'range.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-1025) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-1025) 'RFD66606-1027 permits two formats. bf16 holds one parameter in 2 bytes, and
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-1025) 'Q4_K_M holds one in about 0.55 bytes. The table gives both, per model.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-1025) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-1025) 'The Source column says where each number comes from. `published` means
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-1025) 'the model card states the count. `measured` means this document read
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-1025) 'the checkpoint sizes. `estimated` means this document derives the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-1025) 'count from the architecture. `unknown` means no count is available
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-1025) 'yet.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-1025) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1025  1 LINE
 Text:Written

